<!--
  Identity provider metadata for the SAML screenshots (56, 57, 58). Made up: the
  host is an example domain, nothing answers there, and the certificate below is
  a throwaway (an EC P-256 key that was never kept) valid until November 2056, so
  its expiry never raises the "IdP certificate expires" notice. capture.mjs sends
  this file as pasted XML (the server needs no network for pasted metadata, which
  is why this is not a URL) and strips this comment first, as a real file from an
  identity provider has none. To make a new certificate:
    openssl req -x509 -newkey ec -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:prime256v1 -nodes \
      -keyout /dev/null -out cert.pem -days 11000 -subj "/CN=idp.example.com"
  and put the base64 lines between BEGIN and END into X509Certificate.
-->
